# CSS & Token Conventions

## Three-Layer CSS
1. **`base.css`** — CSS custom properties (design tokens), reset, font imports. Edit here to change global values.
2. **`layout.css`** — Sidebar, page shell, `.page-title`/`.page-sub`, responsive breakpoints. Shared structure.
3. **`components.css`** — Reusable UI pieces: `.scale`, `.step`, `.badge-row`, `.theme-panel`, `.section`, `.placeholder`. Add new component styles here.

## Design Tokens
- Canonical values live in `src/tokens/` as JSON (e.g. `colours.json`)
- CSS variables in `base.css` reference these values
- When adding a new foundation (typography, spacing), create a matching JSON token file

## Key Variables
```css
--page-bg, --ink, --ink-2, --ink-3    /* surface & text hierarchy */
--rule, --card-bg, --radius           /* borders, cards, rounding */
--mono, --serif                       /* font stacks */
--sidebar-w, --sidebar-bg             /* sidebar layout */
```

## Fonts
- **JetBrains Mono** (monospace) — doc site token/code rendering, labels
- **Fraunces** (serif) — headings, page titles, section titles
